 "name": "mpe",
 "title": "MPE for Peak",
 "version": "0.21",
 "label": "MPEL Ver 108.469",
 "summary": "Per-note pitch bend, pressure (channel or poly aftertouch) and slide (MPE) on the Peak's 8 voices, a per-patch MPE switch (VOICE page) and Settings MPE pages; one or two zones. v0.2: the arpeggiator ignores its own notes when a DAW sends them back (MIDI loop). v0.3: turning a knob shows envelope times in ms and the filter cutoff in Hz, with a value bar, and Pickup shows an arrow and a distance bar. v0.4: Settings > MPE > PressCurve chooses stock's squared pressure or a linear curve. v0.5: CC 11 on a member channel works as pressure. v0.6: Settings > MPE EXTRAS > EnvSync sets the amp Decay and Release to a note length (1/2 to 1/16) at the current tempo (v0.7: a changed setting applies after 1 s). v0.8: hold Mod and move a slider or knob to put its modulation destination in the first free matrix slot; the encoder chooses the source. v0.11: Settings > PARAM LOCK keeps the FX, Arp or Voice settings through a patch change. v0.12: Settings > COPY SECTION copies an oscillator, envelope or LFO to another; Mod + Page left/right undoes and redoes the last change; Settings > MIDI MONITOR shows the last message and the DIN overflow count. v0.13: the copy and undo messages stay on screen about 2 s. v0.14: Settings > MPE EXTRAS > Glide starts a poly glide from the previous note (LastNote), or only while another note is held (Legato), instead of from the voice's own last pitch; EnvSync and undo timings corrected. v0.15: the patch's messages always clear and stay 3 s; Msg Time 127 now lasts about 3 s (stock: 1.5 s). v0.16: motion recording: hold Mod and press Animate 1, move a slider or knob, and its movement over one bar loops in time with the tempo (Settings > MOTION sets 1, 2 or 4 bars). v0.17: the recorded movement plays back as a ramp from step to step instead of jumps, also where the loop starts again. v0.18: patch morph: with Settings > MORPH > Morph set to ModWheel, the mod wheel blends the patch as you have edited it (wheel down) towards the patch as it is stored (wheel up); levels, amounts, times, the filter, FX amounts and mod matrix depths move, switches stay. v0.19: morph: holding Compare with the mod wheel up no longer loses the edit when the button is let go; after Save the saved sound is the patch, so the wheel has nothing left to blend until the next edit. v0.20: holding Compare no longer clears the undo step or stops a motion lane: both wait while the button is held and go on when it is let go. Euclidean arp rhythms: Settings > ARP EUCLID sets Pulses, Steps and Rotate, and the arpeggiator plays that many notes spread evenly over the steps in place of the patch's Rhythm. With Arp>MIDI on and no MIDI loop, a key let go just after the arpeggiator's own note off is no longer ignored (before, the arpeggiator could go on playing a released key). v0.21: arp ratchets: Settings > ARP RATCHET makes every note, or every second to eighth one, sound two or three times within its step. Tested on one Peak with the automated hardware test rig and played from a LinnStrument.",
 "built": {
